  "result": "I couldn't find a bug, so I haven't written a plan yet. The repo is Click, and the `--help` code I read matches upstream Click:\n\n- **Option order:** `format_options` in `src/click/core.py` prints options in the order they were declared, with no sorting. `--help` is always appended last.\n- **Decorators:** `src/click/decorators.py` reverses the stacked decorator params so they come out in top-to-bottom source order.\n- **Subcommands:** a `Group` lists them alphabetically, because `list_commands` returns `sorted(self.commands)`.\n- **Tests:** none of them check the order of options in `--help`.\n\nWhich of these is the \"weird order\" you mean?\n\n1. **Click's own behavior.** For example, you want options sorted alphabetically, `--help` shown first, or required options grouped first. If so, tell me the order you expect.\n2. **A specific CLI in this repo**, such as one under `examples/`. If so, tell me which command, and paste its `--help` output if you can.\n3. **Subcommand order in a group.** If so, tell me whether you want declaration order instead of alphabetical.\n\nOnce I know which one, I'll write the plan.",
